# HRMS Project Rules

You are working on a production-grade HR Attendance and Workforce Monitoring System.

Tech stack:
- React + Vite
- Expo React Native
- Supabase
- PostgreSQL
- TypeScript preferred
- Tailwind CSS

Architecture rules:
- Never create duplicate geofence logic
- Always reuse shared utilities
- Keep components under 250 lines
- Separate UI, business logic, and data access
- Use service-layer architecture
- Never store plaintext passwords
- Never use open RLS policies
- Always create migrations for new tables
- Prefer reusable hooks
- Avoid giant components
- Use proper TypeScript types
- Never hardcode fake data in production UI
- Use async error handling everywhere
- Never directly trust client GPS
- Attendance validation must happen server-side
- Prefer Edge Functions for sensitive operations

Folder rules:
- apps/web-admin
- apps/mobile-attendance
- backend/supabase
- backend/edge-functions
- packages/shared

Coding standards:
- Production-grade code only
- No placeholder implementations
- No TODO-only features
- No fake APIs
- No dead code
- No duplicate utilities

Security rules:
- Use Supabase Auth
- Use hashed passwords
- Use JWT/session validation
- Restrict RLS properly
- Never expose admin operations to anon users

Always:
- explain architecture decisions
- explain risks before refactoring
- preserve existing functionality
- generate incremental improvements only